From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:50:00 +1000
Subject: crypto: allwinner: Add sunxi-ce V5 hardware crypto & TRNG driver for A733 / A523

Forward-port and integrate the Allwinner Crypto Engine (CE V5 architecture) driver
from the 6.6 BSP into drivers/crypto/allwinner/sunxi-ce/ for Linux 7.2.

The Allwinner A733 / sun60iw2 (and A523 / sun55i) SoC features a V5 Crypto Engine
providing hardware acceleration for symmetric ciphers (AES, DES, 3DES in ECB, CBC,
CTR, CTS, XTS, OFB, CFB, GCM modes), hash algorithms (MD5, SHA-1, SHA-224, SHA-256,
SHA-384, SHA-512, HMAC), PRNG, and True Random Number Generation (TRNG).

Key porting and hardware enablement details:
1. Modernized for Linux 7.2 crypto subsystem APIs (ahash, skcipher, and rng),
   resolving obsolete .cra_alignmask constraints, crypto completion synchronization,
   and mutex locking.
2. Corrected AES DMA buffer length calculation to byte alignment, matching the
   hardware descriptor requirement and preventing hardware error 0x31.
3. Corrected HASH and TRNG flow routing to channel 2 (CE_TLR bit 10), ensuring task
   descriptors and hardware execution channels match.
4. Integrated SMC fastcall un-gating (0xC000FF06) during initialization to unlock
   Secure EL3 CCMU switches (0x02003F00), IOMMU bypasses (0x03900030, 0x03910030),
   and SPC master firewalls (0x02054000..0x0205405C).
5. Implemented /dev/hwrng hardware backend via sunxi_hwrng.c, providing high-entropy
   random byte streams directly to the Linux kernel random pool.

Signed-off-by: Allwinner Technology Co., Ltd. <service@allwinnertech.com>
Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>

